{
  "track": "es",
  "level": "A1",
  "unit": 12,
  "title": "Shopping",
  "description": "Say what you are buying, and what it costs.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "Shopping in Spanish is two pieces of grammar: ir a + a place to say where you are going, and the word for a price. The verb ir is irregular, so it is worth learning its forms now.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Going to the shop",
        "body": "Ir is one of the most irregular verbs in Spanish: voy, vas, va, vamos, vais, van. After ir you use a instead of de: voy a la tienda, voy al mercado. And the everyday phrase for shopping is ir de compras, not ir a comprar.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "Voy a la tienda.",
            "en": "I am going to the shop."
          },
          {
            "es": "¿Vamos de compras?",
            "en": "Are we going shopping?"
          },
          {
            "es": "Ella va al mercado.",
            "en": "She is going to the market."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Asking the price",
        "body": "The verb for to cost is costar, and it takes the thing first: cuesta diez euros. To ask, put cuánto in front: ¿cuánto cuesta? You can also ask for the price of something specific with cuánto cuesta el abrigo.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "¿Cuánto cuesta?",
            "en": "How much is it?"
          },
          {
            "es": "¿Cuánto cuesta el abrigo?",
            "en": "How much is the coat?"
          },
          {
            "es": "Cuesta veinte euros.",
            "en": "It costs twenty euros."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Saying what you want",
        "body": "Wanting something uses the verb querer, and the thing you want takes un or una: quiero un café, quiero una camisa. If you are asking for something politely, add por favor, which you already know.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "Quiero este sombrero, por favor.",
            "en": "I want this hat, please."
          },
          {
            "es": "¿Buscas algo?",
            "en": "Are you looking for something?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
